Package: psiotropy
Type: Package
Title: An R package for quantifying trade-offs, pleiotropy and genotype-by-environment interactions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Tom", "Ellis", email="thomas.ellis@gmi.oeaw.ac.at", role=c("aut", "cre"))
Maintainer: Tom Ellis <thomas.ellis@thomas.ellis@gmi.oeaw.ac.at>
Description: psiotropy is a package to quantify correlations for single pairs of
    numbers. The motivating use case is understanding genetic pleiotropy, where
    a single gene affects two (or more) traits at once. The input data are pairs
    of numbers describing an effect of Something in two contexts. psiotropy
    calculates the direction of the joint effect in those context as statistic
    $\psi$, and the magnitude $z$ of that effect.
